# xLaDe Runtime State

This document describes how xLaDe manages runtime state across user
environments and individual projects.

It is classified into 2 types:

1. Global State                     (mode)
2. Local State                      (workspace, experiment history, and metrics).

---

## Global State

It exists in `/home/user/` directory as `/.xlade`
It will have an extensionless file called mode.
Mode will record the current mode of CLI set by user.

It will be created automatically after user initialises the project and sets mode.
To delete it, use the command 'xlade clean' from CLI.

---

## Local State

It exists in `xLaDe/` directory as `/.xlade`
It will have total 3 files.

- experiments.lock
- last-run
- metrics.json

First two will be created automatically after initialising the project. 
Third will be created automatically after running an experiment. 

experiments.lock - It records experiment activation state.
last-run         - Contains the ID of the most recently executed experiment.
metrics.json     - A structured JSON array appended on every `xlade run` call.

To delete them, use the same command 'xlade clean' from CLI.

---

## Table summary

| Location                  | Contents                    | Created by   |
|---------------------------|-----------------------------|--------------|
| `~/.xlade/mode`           | Active mode                 | `xlade mode` |
| `.xlade/experiments.lock` | Experiment activation state | `xlade init` |
| `.xlade/last-run`         | Last executed experiment ID | `xlade run`  |
| `.xlade/metrics.json`     | Full structured run history | `xlade run`  |

